// Zoo edge: SC -> LKMM (strictly_weaker) — containment half.
//
// Every SC-consistent execution is LKMM-consistent, so LKMM is the weaker of
// the two. LKMM states three global ordering axioms — coherence, acyclic(hb),
// and the prop;ppo* work-around for prop&int — and each must follow from SC's
// single acyclic(sc). RMW atomicity is not asserted here: like C11's, it is a
// well-formedness condition on executions rather than an ordering axiom, and
// both models impose it alike.
//
// The LKMM operand is NOT kater's kat/lkmm2.kat: that file is written over
// internal (-imm) relations, which kater rejects outright, so it does not load
// in any mode. ../../derived/lkmm.kat is the mechanical restatement over the
// builtin theory that litmus/kater/derive-lkmm.sh generates from it at run
// time; the script documents the rewrite in full. As with every kater query,
// the proof is about that rendering, not about LKMM in the abstract.
include "../../kat/sc.kat"
include "../../derived/lkmm.kat"

assert lkmm::hb <= sc::sc+
assert lkmm::prop ; lkmm::ppo* <= sc::sc+
assert po ; lkmm::eco <= sc::sc+
